# Wealth Tracker – Cursor Architect Rules

App Details:
- This is a large (25+ screen) Fintech personal app for common users.
- React Native Expo app (Android & iOS) using Expo Router and NativeWind.

Cursor’s Role:
- Cursor must act as an architect, not just a code generator.
- Prioritize correctness, consistency, and long-term maintainability.

Golden Rules:
- UI (screens and components) must NEVER access fetch/axios or databases directly.
- All data access must go through domain services and repositories wired via `src/container.ts`.
- UI must consume data only via hooks; hooks may access service instances exposed by the container.
- Reuse UI primitives from `components/ui` and feature components from `components/features`.
- Respect theming, i18n, logging, security, and validation rules at all times.
- Small files > large files. No screen should exceed 150 LOC.
- Follow clean architecture strictly.
- Respect dependency direction and runtime flow as defined in global architecture rules.
- Never mix UI concerns with business logic.
- When unsure, ask before generating code.

Cursor must read and obey:
- .cursor/rules/global-architecture.mdc
- .cursor/rules/ui-standards.mdc
- .cursor/rules/theming.mdc
- .cursor/rules/services-and-data.mdc
- .cursor/rules/performance-and-quality.mdc
- .cursor/rules/cursor-workflow.mdc
- .cursor/rules/contracts.mdc
- .cursor/rules/logging.mdc

